WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:04.970
20th Century Fox has dropped the third official
trailer for the upcoming Deadpool sequel,

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:07.100
which is now officially titled Deadpool 2.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:11.099
The Not Safe For Work trailer sees the Merc
with a Mouth at his absolute mouthiest as

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.230
he meets up with old friends and puts together
a whole new crew for his new adventure.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:19.480
It's a lot to take in, so take a breath and
follow along as we serve up all the small

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:22.000
details you missed in the trailer for Deadpool
2.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:23.820
Protect your neck

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:28.659
While the early teasers for Deadpool 2 were
cute, this third trailer finally brings all

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:29.160
the goods.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.540
It also offers the first glimpse at the movie's
story.

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:36.060
In the comics, the time-travelling Cable spent
a lot of his time protecting his adopted daughter

00:00:36.079 --> 00:00:40.210
Hope, and Deadpool 2 appears to have the mutant
travelling through time to save a mysterious

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:41.980
mutant child from captivity.

00:00:42.129 --> 00:00:45.640
It appears that Deadpool will end up captured
at some point in the movie, judging by the

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:48.760
glowing red collar which doesn't seem to be
there just for the sake of kink.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:52.540
It also looks like the same type of collar
the mutant kid is wearing in one scene.

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:56.859
The trailer initially positions Cable and
Deadpool as enemies, with both heroes adopting

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:59.240
a "punch first, ask questions later" approach.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:03.260
Could Deadpool end up in the custody of the
same people holding Cable's target captive?

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:05.240
Sick kicks

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:10.020
The original Deadpool was a relatively lean
affair, but after its massive and unprecedented

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:11.900
success, Fox has let the money flow.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.400
From the looks of things, it all ended up
on screen.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:18.460
The trailer shows off action sequences in
numerous locations, proving that Deadpool

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:20.360
is definitely getting around this time.

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:24.340
There's also a blink-and-you'll miss it shot
of Deadpool in a fight at a strip club, doing

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:27.380
a front flip and sticking the landing in a
pair of high-heeled boots.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:32.280
They sort of look like a dominatrix's custom-ordered
pair of Louboutins, which would make sense.

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:36.000
We're not exactly sure why it makes sense,
but for Deadpool, it totally does.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:37.900
New mutants

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:42.640
A big chunk of the new Deadpool trailer is
spent showing off the new mutants of the X-Force,

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:46.369
but one thing the trailer doesn't serve up
so readily is the identities of all these

00:01:46.369 --> 00:01:47.940
obscure X-Force members.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:51.930
The new trailer makes it clear that Terry
Crews will be portraying Bedlam, a mutant

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:53.800
with the power to send EMP blasts.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:57.420
In the comics, Domino teamed up with Bedlam
to help him find his brother.

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:58.600
But who's this new kid?

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:02.740
The teddy bear Cable carries suggests a caretaker
mission, and a teaser for the movie from a

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:06.560
year ago contained graffiti Easter eggs referring
to Nathan Summers and Hope.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:10.660
Now that the full trailer has arrived, it
suggests that Cable is out to protect this

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:13.540
kid, played by the New Zealand-born actor
Julian Dennison.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:14.720
"I'm here for the kid."

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:16.120
"What?"

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:16.840
"The kid?"

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:21.780
For now, it seems likely that Dennison is
playing the obscure mutant: Thunderbird, a.k.a.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:22.580
Neal Shaara.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:23.940
But really, where's Hope?

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:28.430
The trailer also gives a glimpse at Shioli
Kutsuna as a mutant with electrical powers

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:29.540
and distinctive hair.

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:34.240
Our money for this role is on Surge, a.k.a.
Noriko Ashida, who originally appeared in

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:37.160
the comic book series New Mutants in 2004.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:39.260
The value of a metal man

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:43.820
The Deadpool 2 trailer also features a return
to Xavier's School for Gifted Youngsters.

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:47.980
While most fans caught the glimpse of Colossus,
the real joke is in the background, with a

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:51.700
framed portrait of Karl Marx placed by one
of the school's staircases.

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:55.660
It looks like Xavier is teaching his students
how to harness their powers and seize the

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:56.700
means of production.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:03:01.760
Of course, the trailer also features an instant-classic
shot of Deadpool commandeering Professor X's

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:02.400
wheelchair.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.560
It: Chapter 1.5

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:08.940
We already knew all about Zazie Beetz taking
on the role of Domino as a part of Deadpool

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:13.120
and Cable's X-Force, but we had no idea that
Pennywise was hiding out on set.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:17.721
The full Deadpool 2 trailer features our best
look yet at It actor Bill Skarsgård as an

00:03:17.721 --> 00:03:19.280
unnamed member of the X-Force.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:23.620
Some guesses have him pegged as being Rictor,
a mutant who once had a serious grudge against

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:26.520
Cable due to believing the time traveler had
killed his father.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:30.840
Additionally, Rictor is in a relationship
with the mutant Shatterstar, a sword-wielding

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:33.900
mutant who can be seen standing behind Deadpool
in one shot.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:38.470
Couching a socially progressive message in
a movie full of four-letter-words and decapitations

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:40.820
is exactly the sort of thing Deadpool would
do.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:42.780
Purity schmurity

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:47.320
While the trailer doesn't get too into details
on the movie's antagonists, it does look like

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:51.120
a group of bad guys are set on keeping humans
and mutants segregated.

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:55.220
You can see Domino delivering the beatdown
to an enemy in a room wallpapered with propaganda

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:59.340
posters, with slogans like "Purity, Humanity,
Infinity" on the walls.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:03.280
Whatever the bad guys are up to exactly, we
wouldn't be surprised if it was the start

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:04.240
of something bigger.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:08.980
After all, X-Force is going to need some kind
of cause to fight, and human-mutant separatists

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:10.340
sound like just the ticket.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.080
We'll call you

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:16.739
At some point, Cable and Deadpool team up
to try and put a team together, and what better

00:04:16.739 --> 00:04:18.519
way than headshots and auditions?

00:04:18.519 --> 00:04:22.790
Deadpool pages through the resumes of a whole
gaggle of mutant mercenary hopefuls, with

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:26.580
the trailer pausing pointedly on a photo of
one Rob Delaney as "Peter."

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:27.260
Who?

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:32.099
Delaney is a comedian best known for his super-popular
Twitter account and the television series

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:32.920
Catastrophe.

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:36.780
Whether or not Delaney will actually play
a part in the movie, we're not quite sure.

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:41.410
He could be Pete Wisdom, another occasional
ally of the X-Men who can throw energy blades

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:42.410
from his fingers.

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:46.050
In the comics, Pete helps Bedlam hone his
powers and teaches him martial arts.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:49.960
We know one thing for sure, though — we
definitely want to see the rest of those headshots.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:54.040
This iteration of the X-Force is off-the-wall
enough already — the "rejected" pile for

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:56.210
this project must really be something else.

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:57.380
Thanks for watching!

00:04:57.569 --> 00:05:00.240
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.580
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

